  "details": "I've got a system on my avatar that allows the head to be scaled with a scale constraint via dynamics, the system was adjusted to turn off the scaling locally (to avoid combating the 0 scaling), but enable it for remote users and locally for any source that isn't the first pass (cameras and mirrors) via VRLabs' mirror detection (`IsLocal` forks between mirror/not mirror by testing a parameter `DetectMirror`, \"not mirror\" sets `DetectMirror` to `true` so that any subsequent execution of this logic falls into the \"mirror\" state, which then drives an animated parameter `IsMirror` to 1, and I use that parameter to control whether the scale constraint is active)\n\nThis system works perfectly fine without any looks applied, and worked perfectly fine during the beta cycle with the Googly Eyes applied to the head (and was pleasantly surprised that the head scaling affected the attached eyes too).\n\nHowever, once the beta concluded and Accessories went live, scaling works for remote users but does not work for me in mirrors and cameras (it still works for the same avatar without a \"look\" applied). I've not performed iterative testing to check what exactly breaks but my suspicion (given that remote scaling still works) is that the mirror detection logic no longer functions as expected.",
